# Issue #224 W1 / N-AL: arc-SEGMENT (line) intersection, circle-line existence
# core.  line_circle_radical_point: foot +- h*u on the circle (foot condition
# kills the cross term).  arc_line_circle_intersect: witness on circumcircle
# (inCircle_R=0, via ArcArcCircles.inCircle_R_zero_of_equidistant) and on the
# line.  3-axiom.  Deferred: arc-sweep + segment t in [0,1] clamp (atan2/float
# oracle layer), b64 layer.
theories/ArcSegmentCircles.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, first proof brick (Stage 2a-curve seam,
# unblocked by #64's arc-line Scope B/C closure).  The offset of a
# circular arc at signed distance d is the CONCENTRIC arc of radius
# r + d: at-distance-d soundness (radial correspondents |d| apart +
# reverse-triangle lower bound over the WHOLE circle, attained -- the
# defining parallel-curve property, valid up to the singularity
# d = -r), tangent parallelism with positive-multiple no-kink form
# (curved analogue of BufferOffset.offset_seg_dir; derivative bridges
# via Rtrigo_reg's derivable_pt_lim_{sin,cos}), tangent-dot = r(r+d)
# giving direction REVERSAL past the singularity, a concrete Qed
# witness that the parallel-curve property FAILS for d < -r
# (inverted-negative-buffer artifact class), and the arc_length
# offset bridge (M-LEN).  No Admitteds.
theories/ArcOffset.v
# Clothoid-aware buffer soundness: the offset of a clothoid's local osculating
# arc is a valid parallel curve when the buffer distance respects the clothoid's
# minimum radius of curvature (1 / max curvature). Bridges the curvature-linear
# spiral (kappa = k0 + (k1-k0)*tau) to arc_offset_dist_exact; the inner buffer
# (d<0) is where the bound bites. Depends on Distance + ArcOffset. Three-axiom.
theories/ClothoidBufferBridge.v
# Issue #64 / D-PT: point-to-circle distance |dist O P - r| (proof companion of
# the ARC_DISTANCE oracle mode).  Reverse-triangle lower bound (every circle point
# >= |dist O P - r|) + radial-foot attainment.  3-axiom.  Deferred: the CircularArc
# sector-clamping (foot in span vs nearest endpoint) and arc-arc distance.
theories/ArcDistance.v
# Issue #64 / JTS #1195 §7 D-AA: arc-to-arc (circle-to-circle) distance, proof
# companion of ARC_ARC_DISTANCE.  Reverse-triangle lower bound through both
# centres (two_circles_dist_lower) + radial-feet attainment (circle_feet_dist),
# composed: externally separated circles are exactly d - r1 - r2 apart
# (two_circles_dist_radial; arc-level arc_arc_dist_external).  Reuses the D-PT
# radial_foot.  3-axiom.  Deferred: on-arc-sector clamp (atan2), internal/
# overlapping regimes, arc-segment distance, b64 layer.
theories/ArcArcDistance.v
# Issue #64 / JTS #1195 §7 D-SL: arc-to-segment (circle-to-line) distance, proof
# companion of ARC_SEGMENT_DISTANCE.  The perpendicular foot is the nearest line
# point (foot_is_nearest_line: dist_sq O (G+t u) = perp^2 + t^2); reverse-triangle
# lower bound (circle_line_dist_lower) + radial-foot attainment over G
# (circle_line_dist_radial = point_circle_dist_radial at P:=G), composed:
# a line outside the circle (r <= perp) is exactly perp - r away
# (arc_segment_dist_external).  Reuses the D-PT radial_foot.  3-axiom.  Deferred:
# on-arc-sector + segment-t clamp (atan2), crossing (=0) regime, b64 layer.
theories/ArcSegmentDistance.v
# Issue #64 / D-PT (full analytical): point-to-ARC distance with sector clamp
# using arc_orient / inCircle_R / arc_span_contains (directedSweep proxy).
# 4-lemmas stub: radial lower + radial attain + foot-on-arc + fallback interface.
# Proof companion for ARC_DISTANCE / COMPOUND_ARC_DISTANCE RocqRefRunner pin.
# 3-axiom (reuses ArcDistance). Chord-approx Option B.
# Banks the circle/dot monotonicity helpers (all Qed) and isolates the single
# residual planar single-peak dot bound (arc_dot_max_at_endpoint) that the
# point-to-arc fallback reduces to.  Must precede ArcPointDistance.v.
theories/ArcSinglePeak.v
theories/ArcPointDistance.v

# The LEC ARC row (ledger rung "point-to-arc spec" closed + failed path F4).
# Glues ArcPointDistance's case lemmas into the TOTAL closed form arc_dist
# (centre / radial-in-span / endpoint fallback) and proves it exact with no
