# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 2: the SQL/MM three-point bridge.
# radial_offset (homothety about the center, pure rational arithmetic,
# no trig) carries ArcOffset's parallel-curve property into coordinate
# form (radial_offset_dist_exact); circumcenter UNIQUENESS
# (equidistant_point_is_arc_center -- the converse of
# ArcChordApprox.arc_center_equidistant that CurveGeometry.v's comment
# deferred); and the closure headline arc_offset_preserves_arc: the
# radial offset of a valid three-point CircularArc is again a valid
# three-point CircularArc with the SAME arc_center and arc_radius = r+d
# ("buffer/offset preserving arcs" at the representation level), plus
# per-control-point at-distance-|d| facts.  No Admitteds.
theories/ArcOffsetThreePoint.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 3: segment-wise offset of a
# COMPOUNDCURVE ring (chords via BufferOffset.offset_point, arcs via
# arc_offset_arc).  Arc validity survives under the per-arc safety
# bound (curve_ring_offset_arcs_valid); G1 joins with CONSISTENT
# normals offset continuously (arc_join_offset_continuous, the
# no-join-edge-needed case); and the honest negative
# tangent_continuity_insufficient_for_offset -- a concrete S-curve
# (inflection) witness where tangent-line continuity holds but the
# offset TEARS (anti-parallel normals), the arc-side reason stage-2b
# join edges remain necessary (JTS#1147 / OffsetCurve artifact class).
# No Admitteds.
theories/CurveRingOffset.v
# Clothoid-clothoid offset contact soundness (adjacent pair): the reusable
# internal-tangency uniqueness engine (two circles at centre distance |r1-r2|,
# r1<>r2, meet at one point) + the intended G1 join contact surviving the offset.
# Depends on ArcOffsetThreePoint + ArcArcSound + CurveRingOffset + ArcArcCircles.
# Three-axiom.
theories/ClothoidOffsetContact.v

# Global clothoid offset assembly soundness (adjacency level, whole ring):
# lifts ClothoidOffsetContact's pairwise "meet only at join" over a closed
# clothoid arc-ring -- every consecutive offset-arc pair (interior + wrap) is a
# single clean contact, and the offset ring is valid (clothoid_ring_offset_valid).
# Depends on CurveRingOffset + ClothoidOffsetContact + ClothoidBufferBridge.
# Three-axiom.
theories/ClothoidBufferAssembly.v

# Offset-ring simplicity from clearance (the global, non-adjacent half): a valid,
# safely-offset CurveRing whose non-adjacent source segments have pairwise
# clearance > 2|d| offsets to a curve_ring_simple ring (a metric tube argument:
# every offset point is within |d| of its source segment -- chords parallel,
# arcs radial). Covers chords + arcs, so clothoid arc-rings included.
# Depends on ArcOffsetThreePoint + ArcArcCircles + BufferOffset + CurveRingOffset
# + CurveRingSimple. Three-axiom.
theories/CurveRingOffsetSimple.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 5: the ROUND JOIN ARC in SQL/MM
# three-point form -- the join edge CurveRingOffset's tear witness
# forces at non-G1 joins, emitted AS AN ARC.  unit_cross_nonzero (the
# turning lemma: distinct non-antipodal unit vectors are not parallel);
# round_join_arc_valid (control-point cross factors as
# d^2 (2-h)/h cross(n1,n2), h=|n1+n2| -- a valid CircularArc);
# round_join_arc_center_radius (circumcircle is EXACTLY (P,|d|), via
# rung 2's circumcenter uniqueness); round_join_connects (endpoints
# coincide with the adjacent offset segments' endpoints, via rung 4's
# uniform normal field); plus unit-ness of the ring's own normal
# fields.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveRoundJoin.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 6 (assembly capstone): splice the
# round-join arcs into the segment-wise offset ring.  offset_walk /
# curve_ring_offset_round walk the ring emitting each segment's offset
# plus, at every join a supplied G1 decision flags non-smooth, the
# CurveRoundJoin arc (incl. the closing join); the decision is an
# abstract boolean oracle with a correctness spec (real equality is
# not computable; extraction supplies the comparison).  Headline
# curve_ring_offset_round_valid: for a valid ring with nondegenerate
# chords, offset within the per-arc safety bound, d <> 0, and no
# U-turn (anti-parallel-normal) joins, the assembled output is again
# a valid_curve_ring -- extending rung 4's smooth-ring capstone to
# arbitrary non-U-turn compound rings.  Coherence:
# offset_walk_smooth_eq_map (on all-G1 rings the walk equals rung 3's
# plain map).  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveOffsetAssembly.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 7: the SEMICIRCLE arc -- one SQL/MM
# construction closing both remaining join/cap gaps: the U-TURN join the
# assembly excluded (anti-parallel normals, semicircle_uturn_connects)
# and the ROUND ENDCAP for open compound lines (+d boundary around the
# end to the -d boundary, semicircle_cap_connects).  Validity via
# Vec.lagrange_identity (cross(t,n)^2 = 1 for unit perpendicular t, n;
# control-point cross = -2 d^2 cross(t,n)); circumcircle EXACTLY (P,|d|)
# via the circumcenter-uniqueness lemma (third consumer); canonical
# sweep direction cap_tangent := vperp with unit/perp dischargers.
# No Admitteds.
theories/CurveSemicircle.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 8: TOTAL assembly -- the offset
# ring with NO join exclusions.  join_connector is the three-way join
# policy (G1: nothing; U-turn: rung 7's semicircle with a supplied
# sweep side tsel; otherwise: the round join), with uturndec a second
# spec'd boolean oracle and tsel spec'd unit-perpendicular (canonical
# instance vperp, tsel_vperp_spec).  Headline
# curve_ring_offset_total_valid: ANY valid compound ring with
# nondegenerate chords, offset within the per-arc safety bound, d <> 0
# assembles -- offset segments + connectors incl. the closing join --
# into a valid_curve_ring; no U-turn or turning hypotheses remain.
# Coherence offset_walk_total_smooth_eq_map as before.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveOffsetAssemblyTotal.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 9 (forward pointer P1): the SQL/MM
# hierarchy lift.  curve_polygon_offset / curve_geometry_offset apply
# the rung-8 total ring assembly to the outer ring and every hole (one
# signed d for all rings; the side is encoded by ring orientation
# through the normal field, the JTS OffsetCurveBuilder convention).
# Headlines curve_{polygon,geometry}_offset_valid: validity preserved
# at every hierarchy level under the bundled per-ring side conditions
# (polygon_offsetable) and d <> 0 -- complete w.r.t. the corpus's
# validity layer (hole-inside-outer is deliberately punted to the
# analytic layer per CurveGeometry §4, tracked as P2).  Plus
# hole/polygon count preservation.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurvePolygonOffset.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 10 (forward pointer P10 brick 1):
# certified rational decision procedures for the assembly oracles.
# Unit-normal EQUALITY is a rational condition on the un-normalised
# vectors (unit_eq_iff_cross_dot: u^=v^ <-> cross=0 /\ 0<dot; opp
# variant for anti-parallel), the ring's normal fields normalise from
# RATIONAL raw normals (vperp of the direction / P - arc_center), and
# the headlines g1_decision_correct / uturn_decision_correct show the
# rung-6/8/9 g1dec and uturndec specs are realizable by one exact-Q
# cross and dot each.  offset_safe_iff_sq decides the safety bound
# from the rational r^2.  The OCaml CURVE_JOIN_CLASSIFY mode (brick 2)
# is deferred to a CI-buildable session.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveJoinClassify.v
# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 11 (forward pointer P3): the
# stage-2 -> stage-3 handoff.  The curve front-end's chord case IS
# BufferOffset.offset_seg (definitional coherence with the linear
# stage-2a seam); the segment-wise map preserves all-chord rings; and
# the headline offset_emit_ring_closed composes rung 8's validity with
# CurveLinearise.chord_approx_ring_closed: the assembled offset ring's
# chord linearisation is a ring_closed Phase-3 ring -- the emitted
# edge list CLOSES, the structural contract stage 3 (noding) needs.
# linear_offset_emit_ring_closed specialises to all-chord input,
# discharging the round-join flavour of the linear emitted-edge-list
# gap (miter/bevel join emission and open-chain caps remain honestly
# open).  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveOffsetEmit.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 12: the BEVEL assembly -- the
# join-edge flavour rung 11 left open, emitted as CHORDS.  bevel_join
# is the chord across the tear (splice facts definitional); it handles
# every non-G1 join uniformly, U-turns included, and contributes
# nothing to arc validity -- so curve_ring_offset_bevel_valid carries
# the LEANEST hypothesis set of the three assemblies (ring validity +
# per-arc safety + the G1-decision spec only).  Plus
# bevel_join_nondeg (quality), all-chord preservation (the pure linear
# bevel emitter), the stage-3 handoff bevel_emit_ring_closed, and the
# smooth-case coherence.  MITER emission (via BufferMiter.miter_apex)
# remains the one open join flavour.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveBevelJoin.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 13: the MITER assembly -- the last
# open join flavour of the 2b row, emitted as two chords through
# BufferMiter.miter_apex (the JTS#180 Cramer's-rule offset-line
# intersection), with rung 12's bevel as the fallback at joins
# involving arcs (JTS miters only line corners).  Connectors are
# chords with definitional splices, so curve_ring_offset_miter_valid
# keeps the bevel assembly's lean hypothesis set; the geometric tie-in
# miter_connector_apex_sound attaches the perpendicular-distance-d
# property to the emitted apex.  Plus all-chord preservation (the pure
# linear miter emitter), the stage-3 handoff, smooth coherence, and
# generic hd/last/app chain-gluing bricks.  The 2b join EMISSION story
# (round / bevel / miter) is now complete.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveMiterJoin.v
# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 14a: the REVERSAL layer for the
# open-chain cap walk (14b) and the SQL/MM ring-orientation flip.
# rev_arc / rev_segment / curve_ring_reverse; circumcircle invariance
# under reversal (rev_arc_center via circumcenter uniqueness, its 4th
# consumer; rev_arc_radius, rev_arc_valid); the ORIENTATION WART made
# formal: arc radial normals are traversal-agnostic but chord
# unit_perp normals FLIP, so offset/reverse commute at OPPOSITE signs
# per kind (offset_rev_chord at -d, offset_rev_arc at +d) -- why JTS
# tracks an explicit side flag.  Headline valid_curve_ring_reverse:
# ring reversal preserves compound-ring validity.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveReverse.v

# Issue #65 curve-aware buffer, rung 14b: the OPEN-CHAIN two-sided cap
# walk -- the last structural emission gap.  chain_walk (open: offsets
# + chord connectors, no closing join); rung-7 semicircle caps at both
# ends (cap_far via semicircle_cap_connects, cap_start the mirror);
# the right boundary is curve_ring_reverse (chain_walk (-d) c), so the
# 14a reversal lemmas supply all its structure and no per-kind sign
# threading is needed (the orientation-wart-dictated design).
# Headline curve_chain_buffer_valid: a nonempty adjacent chain with
# valid arcs, nondegenerate chords, two-sided safety and d <> 0
# assembles into a CLOSED valid compound ring -- the buffer boundary
# of an open compound line.  Every stage-2 emission (rings AND chains)
# now produces a valid compound ring.  No Admitteds.
theories/CurveCapWalk.v

# Issue #65 / JTS #1195 §7 (BUF-1 / BUF-NEG): the buffer-region AREA companion of
# the BUFFER_REGION oracle (assemble offset boundary + signed area).  Per-arc
# buffer segment area buffer_arc_area = segment_area (r+d); d=0 identity;
# buffer_arc_area_grows (outward buffer grows each arc's segment area); reuse of
# offset_safe_iff_sq (rational EMPTY decision), curve_ring_offset_arcs_valid
# (boundary validity), arc_offset_dist_exact (the parallel-distance property).
# 3-axiom [exact] (segment_area magnitude uses ArcLength.sin_le_x).  The
# geometric "signed area = true Minkowski buffer area" is the deferred P2 frontier,
# pinned by oracle/gen_buffer_region_tests.py.
theories/CurveBufferArea.v

# Flocq-dependent modules (built only in the container; require coq-flocq).
# Live in theories-flocq/ rather than theories/ so the host CI grep for
# Admitted markers does not pick up in-progress soundness bridges.
-Q theories-flocq NTS.Proofs.Flocq
theories-flocq/Validate_binary64.v
theories-flocq/Orientation_b64.v
# binary64 <-> R bridge.  Lifts Flocq's Bplus_correct / Bminus_correct /
# Bmult_correct to b64_plus / b64_minus / b64_mult under a no-overflow
# precondition.  Critical-path module identified in
# docs/audit-shewchuk-stages.md: unlocks the simplifier R-bridge, the
# orient2d arithmetic identities, and Shewchuk Stages B/C of orient2d.
theories-flocq/B64_bridge.v
# Forward-looking wrapper module.  Promotes the `Local Notation b64_*`
# boilerplate to module-level, registers Flocq typeclass instances for
# binary64 (Prec_gt_0, Valid_exp, Monotone_exp), and re-exports
# pre-instantiated Flocq lemmas (ulp_le_abs, ulp_FLT_0,
# error_le_half_ulp_round, etc.) plus helpers accumulated during
# Stage D (round_minus_swap, etc.).  Placed here -- right after its
# upstream B64_bridge -- so downstream files (Orient_b64_exact,
# Intersect_b64_exact_core, HotPixel_b64) can `Require Import B64_lib`
# instead of repeating the Local Notation boilerplate.
theories-flocq/B64_lib.v
# R-side arithmetic identities for b64_orient2d, proved via composition
# of the per-op lifts in B64_bridge.  First downstream consumer of the
# bridge; establishes the pattern other identities will reuse.
