# core = slices 1-5 (on-grid reduction, fixed-point grid, slab guards,
# coordinate exactness, max/min bridge); bounds = slices 6-8 (division
# bridge, correctly-rounded t-bounds, clipped bounds); complete = slices
# 9-11 (on-grid completeness, conditional headline, rounding reflection);
# gap_kernel = slices 12-13 (rational-gap + ulp upper bound -- B4's
# off-list exit corrected 2026-08-16: the slice-13 ulp lemmas mention
# b64_round in their statements and carry classic, so the file is
# re-listed; slice-12 lemmas machine-verified clean);
# separation = slices 14-18 (gap-beats-band, gridbound, the unconditional
# tight-grid headline).  The umbrella re-exports all five, so the two
# reverse dependencies import unchanged.
